#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:252 c5960a52896146a4ae7b7109503cae9d
msgid ""
"When a user in a source VM executes ``qrexec-client-vm`` utility, the "
"following steps are taken:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:254 5aaf672ca57f4851be1dc80f070a0d19
msgid ""
"``qrexec-client-vm`` connects to ``qrexec-agent``’s ``/var/run/qubes/qrexec-"
"agent-fdpass`` unix socket 3 times. Reads 4 bytes from each of them, which "
"is the fd number of the accepted socket in agent. These 3 integers, in text, "
"concatenated, form “connection identifier” (CID)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:256 90be1eb0d2ec470b86e5e2fe92d7e23c
msgid ""
"``qrexec-client-vm`` writes to ``/var/run/qubes/qrexec-agent`` fifo a blob, "
"consisting of target vmname, rpc action, and CID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:258 f0d4901f1d5d46a6b396625250b0cc73
msgid ""
"``qrexec-client-vm`` executes the rpc client, passing the above mentioned "
"unix sockets as process stdin/stdout, and optionally stderr (if the "
"``PASS_LOCAL_STDERR`` env variable is set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:260 a02a27de7ed546fea0ac5907595c2aa5
msgid ""
"``qrexec-agent`` passes the blob to ``qrexec-daemon``, via "
"``MSG_AGENT_TO_SERVER_TRIGGER_CONNECT_EXISTING`` message over vchan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:262 e2623be3db3e4f159d3e754d6ef0b6da
msgid ""
"``qrexec-daemon`` executes ``qrexec-policy``, passing source vmname, target "
"vmname, rpc action, and CID as cmdline arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:264 2d928e253e7746d29624d7af4f2cfd1f
msgid ""
"``qrexec-policy`` evaluates the policy file. If successful, creates a pair "
"of ``qrexec-client`` processes, whose stdin/stdout are cross-connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:266 dffbb7d7d94d4973998080fe10c9905e
msgid ""
"The first ``qrexec-client`` connects to the src VM, using the ``-c "
"ClientID`` parameter, which results in not creating a new process, but "
"connecting to the existing process file descriptors (these are the fds of "
"unix socket created in step 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:268 e22061a747694c5fbe2660e52f40b376
msgid ""
"The second ``qrexec-client`` connects to the target VM, and executes ``qubes-"
"rpc-multiplexer`` command there with the rpc action as the cmdline argument. "
"Finally, ``qubes-rpc-multiplexer`` executes the correct rpc server on the "
"target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:272 69c6d73ff5164e3dbc250d8ac3034b35
msgid ""
"In the above step, if the target VM is ``$dispvm``, the DispVM is created "
"via the ``qfile-daemon-dvm`` program. The latter waits for the ``qrexec-"
"client`` process to exit, and then destroys the DispVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec2.rst:276 2e43b7a03f0d459e84249522689fd41e
msgid "*TODO: Protocol description (“wire-level” spec)*"
msgstr ""
